From 068960d1d4b42c1e1f304f91d703ade7330c72b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:25:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Every headless cold resume leaves a paused turn to
 the restarting backend; the window covers the hand-off

Follow-up to aa3a75eb9da (PR 1278): _wake_session_turn yields a turn paused for a
Hermes update to the dead writer's successor, so its continuation and re-asked
clarify form run where the chat's viewers attach. Two gaps were left.

1. Two more producers resume an unloaded chat in-process with no viewer and took
   the continuation the same way (session.resume schedules it):
   - producer_admission._sweep_owner (every `hermes serve`/dashboard process,
     every 15 s): now returns verdict "paused_turn" while
     successor_owes_continuation holds; the row stays queued for the next pass.
   - _wake_chat_for_readopted_exit (each Desktop-owned backend sharing the home):
     its parked exit is lost if it gives up, so it waits the hand-off out
     (update_pause.wait_out_successor, rereading every 5 s), then resumes as
     before unless the chat was loaded here meanwhile.

2. The window (135 s from the pause stamp) ended before the successor arrived.
   hermes-hub gui.log, 2026-10-30..11-12, 81 continuations of a dead writer's
   pause: scheduled 11-2781 s after the stamp (50 at or past 135 s), because a
   writer holds its pause until the update applies. Against the checkout's
   reflog the schedule came 42-198 s after the move; with no move, up to 545 s
   after the stamp. The window now counts from this process's own start when it
   started after the pause (it restarted in the same update): SUCCESSOR_YIELD_S
   = 300 s. A reader that did not restart cannot date the writer's exit and
   counts from the stamp: SUCCESSOR_YIELD_UNKNOWN_S = 660 s. Past either, any
   reader continues, as before.

The wake's log line moved with the predicate to tui_gateway.update_pause
(left_to_successor), keeping session_notifications.py at its line cap.

RED on 2ff7a5cadbe (production files reverted): 6 of 7 tests in
test_cold_resume_yields_paused_turn.py fail, "the sweep took the paused turn's
continuation" / "the wake took the paused turn's continuation".
GREEN: 92 files importing the changed modules, 1195 passed.
